    "result_text": "The full build passes. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `membershipTier` field on the owner response, following the project's OfficeFloor/OpenAPI conventions:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a derived mapping (same `@Named` qualifier pattern as the existing `displayName`/`initials` computed fields) that returns `\"SILVER\"` when `namesakeCount == 0` and an email is present, otherwise `\"BRONZE\"`.\n\nSince the tier is computed in the mapper at read time, both `GET /api/owners/{id}` and the create response get it automatically. Tests pass: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail` (SILVER) and `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail` (BRONZE), plus BUILD SUCCESS for the full run.",
